# Deloitte Australia Data Analytics Job Simulation

## Project Overview
This project was completed as part of the Deloitte Australia Data Analytics Job Simulation on Forage.

The project involved analysing operational telemetry data and compensation equality data for Daikibo Industrials.

## Objectives

The analysis focused on two major business areas:

### 1. Factory Machine Downtime Analysis
Daikibo collected telemetry data from four factories:

- Daikibo Factory Meiyo – Tokyo, Japan
- Daikibo Factory Seiko – Osaka, Japan
- Daikibo Berlin – Berlin, Germany
- Daikibo Shenzhen – Shenzhen, China

The objective was to answer:

- Which factory experienced the most machine downtime?
- Which device types experienced the most downtime within that factory?

Each machine sent telemetry information every 10 minutes. An unhealthy status was therefore treated as 10 minutes of potential downtime.

### 2. Gender Pay Equality Analysis
Daikibo also requested an investigation into potential gender pay inequality across factories and job roles.

Equality scores ranged from -100 to +100, with 0 representing ideal equality.

Scores were classified as:

- Fair: -10 to +10
- Unfair: -20 to -11 and +11 to +20
- Highly Discriminative: below -20 or above +20

